NOTICE for @magpie-community/page-digital-pet
=============================================

This package is a magpie page/plugin adapter. It does not bundle the upstream
engine itself; the engine is an external npm dependency:
@jcendal/opencode-digital-pet 0.18.0 (Apache License 2.0), by Jorge Cendal
(jcendal) and Sergio Bugallo (sbugallo). At runtime that package is installed
by the package manager; it is not vendored into this repository.

The sidebar page's pixel sprite frames (lib/monster-frames.json) are extracted
from that same Apache-2.0 upstream package's TUI bundle
(MONSTER_FRAME_DATA, jcendal/digital-pet 0.18.0) by tools/extract-frames.mjs,
and are redistributed here under the same Apache License 2.0. Sprites without
a catalog entry fall back to a deterministic procedural pixel blob.

The sidebar page additionally renders hi-def PNG sprite frames for 474 species
(sprites/ directory, local-only, not distributed with this repository) sourced
from sundeth/omnipet (https://github.com/sundeth/omnipet), licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0),
© Anderson Porto 2025. The omnipet sprites are in turn derived from
Tortoiseshel's Full Color Digimon Dot Sprites
(https://withthewill.net/threads/22970-Full-Color-Digimon-Dot-Sprites).
Frame semantics (idle/walk/attack/happy/eat/sleep/injured) are decoded from
the omnipet sprite atlas convention. Species without a PNG mapping continue
to use the Apache-2.0 text frames or the procedural fallback.

